  "interpretation": "<p><strong data-start=\"61\" data-end=\"70\">HBeAg</strong> is a secreted viral protein found in the blood during active replication of the <strong data-start=\"151\" data-end=\"178\">Hepatitis B virus (HBV)</strong>. It is typically used to assess <strong data-start=\"211\" data-end=\"226\">infectivity</strong>, <strong data-start=\"228\" data-end=\"256\">viral replication status</strong>, and to monitor <strong data-start=\"273\" data-end=\"306\">response to antiviral therapy</strong>.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Result</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Positive (Detected)</strong></td>\n<td>Indicates <strong>active HBV replication</strong> and <strong>high infectivity</strong>. The patient is likely in the <strong>immune-tolerant or immune-active phase</strong> of chronic HBV.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Negative (Not Detected)</strong></td>\n<td>Suggests <strong>low or absent HBV replication</strong>. May indicate <strong>inactive carrier state</strong>, <strong>immune control</strong>, or <strong>precore mutant infection</strong>.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Clinical Context</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>HBsAg</strong></th>\n<th><strong>HBeAg</strong></th>\n<th><strong>HBV DNA</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Likely Status</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Positive</td>\n<td>Positive</td>\n<td>High</td>\n<td>Active infection, highly infectious</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Positive</td>\n<td>Negative</td>\n<td>Low or Undetectable</td>\n<td>Inactive carrier or resolved infection</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Positive</td>\n<td>Negative</td>\n<td>High</td>\n<td>Precore or basal core promoter mutant infection</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
